[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="ManualPage" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/components/manual_page.gd" id="1_page"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_page")
title = "POWER"
body = "GENERATION is a 500 W RTG. The battery holds 4000 Wh. Circuits are ranked by priority; when demand exceeds supply the ship sheds the least critical circuit first.

PRIORITY ORDER (least critical sheds first)
  LIFE SUPPORT is never shed
  LIGHTING sheds before the SCRUBBER

CABIN LIGHTS. SHIP CONTROL / LIGHTING switches each cabin, service bay, installed pod and exterior work light separately. Cabin and pod fixtures draw 25 W each; the two exterior work lights draw 10 W each. Two unused cabin lights off save 50 Wh per hour. The master LIGHTING breaker still isolates them all; restoring it preserves your individual choices.

ALL LIGHTS ON is possible while the battery covers demand above the RTG's 500 W output. On the bare ship the twelve interior fixtures and two exterior beams draw 320 W. Switch off unused rooms to stretch the battery; keep maintenance spaces lit and use the handheld torch for dark rooms.

BROWNOUT. When generation and available battery power cannot meet demand, the ship sheds the least critical circuits until the remaining loads fit. Priority 0 is never shed, but still needs available power. Take non-essential circuits offline at the breaker panel before the battery empties.

WHEN A CIRCUIT IS SHED it returns automatically only when generation can carry the remaining loads plus that circuit with 25 W to spare. Recharged battery power does not trigger automatic restoration. Switch off unused lights or isolate non-essential circuits to free sustained headroom; repair faults that reduce generation.

LIGHTING FAULT. Do not confuse switched-off lights with failed hardware. With breakers on, check STATUS and use the multimeter at the POWER test point in storage. For LIGHTING BALLAST, turn only LIGHTING OFF in SHIP CONTROL / POWER (or use the storage lighting breaker). Carry the wrench to POWER: OPEN LIGHTING BALLAST COVER, REFIT LIGHTING BALLAST (one gasket from stores), CLOSE LIGHTING BALLAST COVER. Restore LIGHTING; verify the failure clears and enabled lamps work. Individual light choices remain unchanged. See DIAGNOSTICS for RTG/battery ALL-bus isolation."
